# SomnoTrace — pinned static-analysis tool versions
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A linter's finding set is a function of its VERSION, and that is
# measured here rather than assumed: between cppcheck 2.13.0 and 2.19.0, on this very
# tree, the SAME false positive is reported under two different check ids
# (`comparePointers` vs `subtractPointers`), 2.19 reports one that 2.13 does not, and the
# advisory style count is 103 vs 126. A contributor who installs "cppcheck" from their own
# distro and gets a different answer from CI has no way to tell whether they broke
# something or merely have a newer analyser. This file is what makes that answerable.
#
# These are the versions GitHub's `ubuntu-latest` image ships today, and the versions every
# number in the lint proposal was measured against. They are DESCRIPTIVE, not enforced:
# `apt-get install cppcheck` takes whatever the image has, and pinning an exact apt
# revision would break the build the day Ubuntu rebuilds the package for unrelated reasons
# — trading a clear signal for an unrelated outage.
#
# The workflow compares what it got against these and prints a WARNING on a mismatch, so a
# runner image bump is visible in the log of the run that first sees it instead of being
# discovered as an unexplained new finding weeks later. If a bump does change the verdict:
# re-measure, update this file in the same commit, and say what moved.
#
# To reproduce CI exactly on any machine, regardless of what your distro ships:
#   ./scripts/lint.sh --docker
# which runs the pinned image rather than your local tools.

# The distro package the runner installs (dpkg -s cppcheck | grep ^Version)
CPPCHECK_VERSION=2.13.0
CPPCHECK_APT_VERSION=2.13.0-2ubuntu3

# shellcheck --version
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.9.0
SHELLCHECK_APT_VERSION=0.9.0-1

# The image both the workflow and ./scripts/lint.sh --docker resolve the above from.
LINT_IMAGE=ubuntu:24.04

# Measured against these versions on main @ 1ac2d48 (2026-09-06):
#   cppcheck blocking tier (error/warning/performance/portability) : 0 after 2 inline suppressions
#   cppcheck advisory style tier                                   : 103
#   shellcheck --severity=warning over our 3 scripts               : 0 after the SC2164 fix
#   shellcheck note-level (SC2086) over the same scripts           : 7
